  m_text: "A Decal Projector projects a material along its box's blue (Z) axis onto the surfaces inside the box; the meshes do not change. Decal Layers choose which surfaces receive it: the decal draws only on objects that share one of its Rendering Layers. This rust stain points down at the floor.\n\n<b>Predict:</b> The figure stands inside the decal's box. Will the rust stain appear on the figure?\n\n<b>Try:</b>\n1. Select Decal - Rust stain and look at its box in the Scene view.\n2. Select the figure's four parts (Body, Head, Leg L, Leg R) and add Light Layer 1 to their Rendering Layer Mask.\n3. Change the decal's Width, Height and Projection Depth.\n\n<size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: Unity basics: GameObjects-And-Components, 7 \xB7 Rendering Layers</color></size>"
